<Base title="About — ACTA FRAGILIA" lang="en">
  <article class="page-content">
    <header class="page-header">
      <h1>About the Project</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lead">
        ACTA FRAGILIA is an independent platform for long-form journalism, document analysis, and investigations in the fields of law, economics, corporate conflicts, and social processes.
      </p>

      <h2>Principles</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Fact-checking.</strong> Every claim is verified against primary sources.</li>
        <li><strong>Context over sensation.</strong> We analyze systemic causes, not isolated cases.</li>
        <li><strong>Attention to consequences.</strong> We ask: who bears the cost of decisions made?</li>
        <li><strong>No news cycle pressure.</strong> Texts are published when they are ready, not when the news agenda demands.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Methodology</h2>
      <p>
        Materials are based on court documents, regulatory filings, corporate registries, and direct interviews. Where possible, we publish links to sources or scans of documents.
      </p>

      <h2>Language</h2>
      <p>
        The project publishes in Russian, English, Polish, and Belarusian. Not all materials are available in all languages — priority is given to the language most relevant to the subject.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
